# UI Design Rules

Apply these rules to any HTML/template/CSS written for this project. The system is Bootstrap
5.3.3 following the OS light/dark preference (`$color-mode-type: media-query` — no
`data-bs-theme`, no toggle), plus a small custom layer in
`app/assets/stylesheets/refresh.scss`.

## Core principles

1. **Color encodes meaning, not category.** Reserve color for: red = danger/error, amber =
   attention/warning, green = success/printing-normally, blue = active/selected/link. If color
   isn't telling the user something specific, it shouldn't be there. Printers and jobs already
   have real states worth coloring — don't spend color on anything else.

2. **Dim the common case so outliers pop.** When most values in a column are identical
   (statuses, durations, printer names), render the common case in muted gray and let
   exceptions stand out. A wall of green tells the user nothing; one amber row does.

3. **One primary action per region.** At most one filled `btn-primary` per page region.
   Everything else is `btn-outline-secondary`.

4. **Pages should do work, not just present data.** Surface counts that need attention inline.
   The dashboard's job is to answer "is anything wrong, and is my print done?" at a glance
   from across the room.

5. **Density beats whitespace.** This is a shop tool. Body text is 12-13px in tables. Tighten
   padding aggressively. The dashboard is the exception — it is read at a distance and may
   run larger.

6. **Both color modes must work.** Use Bootstrap CSS variables (`var(--bs-body-bg)`,
   `var(--bs-secondary-color)`) and utility classes (`text-body`, `text-secondary`,
   `text-bg-*-subtle`) rather than literal colors.

## Buttons

- `btn-primary` — the single most-used action per region only.
- `btn-outline-secondary` — everything else.
- `btn-danger` / `btn-outline-danger` — only for genuinely destructive actions (Delete a
  printer, discard a print). Destructive buttons belong in a `⋯` kebab menu, never bare.
- Never use `btn-success` / `btn-warning` / `btn-info` as category color labels. Semantic
  meaning only.

## Status indicators

- Most rows sharing a status → a 6px colored dot (`.status-dot` with `.status-success`,
  `.status-danger`, `.status-warning`, `.status-muted`), no label.
- Exceptional statuses → a small `text-bg-*-subtle` badge with a label.
- Never use saturated `bg-success` / `bg-danger` filled badges. Always the `-subtle` variants.
- ALL CAPS status pills are forbidden. Sentence case only.
- Printer connectivity has its own partial (`printers/_prusalink_status_dot`) that the live
  broadcaster re-renders — reuse it rather than inlining another dot.

## Numbers, durations, and temperatures

- Right-align numeric columns with `class="num"` (tabular figures).
- Zero values: `text-secondary` (muted).
- Outlier values in a column of similar values: add `fw-medium`.
- Never wrap counts in colored badges (`<span class="badge bg-info">42</span>`). Plain numerals.
- Durations read as "4h 12m", not seconds or decimal hours. Temperatures carry a degree unit
  and one decimal at most.

## Dates

- Today: time only ("3:05 AM")
- Yesterday: "Yesterday"
- Within 7 days: "3 days ago"
- Same year: "Apr 27"
- Different year: "Apr 27, 2025"
- Full timestamp goes in the `title` attribute for hover precision.
- System/audit timestamps (last polled, updated, created) are 12px muted and grouped at the
  bottom of the page, not mixed in with content.
- Timestamps render in the `TIMEZONE` env zone — use the app's date helpers, don't format
  `Time` objects inline.

## Filters

- Multiple filters → `.filter-chip` components in flex-wrap rows, with `.active` on the
  currently applied one.
- Show an "X filters active · Clear" indicator when filters are applied.

## Tables

- Apply `.table-compact` for 13px text and tight padding.
- Headers: 11px uppercase muted with letter-spacing (`.h-section-label` is the same treatment
  for section headings).
- Whole rows clickable when there's a detail view — no separate Details button.
- One outline action button max per row. Multiple actions → kebab menu.
- Status columns: dot, not pill (see above).
- Long lists need pagination past ~50 rows (Pagy is already wired up).

## Page header pattern

```erb
<div class="d-flex align-items-end justify-content-between mb-3">
  <div>
    <h1 class="h-page-title mb-0">Jobs</h1>
    <div class="text-13 text-secondary mt-1">
      <span class="text-body"><%= total %></span> total ·
      <span class="text-success"><%= active %></span> printing
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="d-flex gap-2">
    <%= link_to '+ Add printer', new_printer_path, class: 'btn btn-primary btn-sm' %>
    <%= link_to 'Reports', reports_path, class: 'btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm' %>
  </div>
</div>
```

## Viewer tiers

The same page is seen by four kinds of viewer (anonymous off-network, anonymous on
`INTERNAL_NETWORKS`, logged-in user, admin). Layer affordances onto one shared page rather
than building separate pages per tier: hero, filters, and table columns stay in the same
positions, and higher tiers gain controls. Gate them on `logged_in?`, `admin?`,
`internal_network?`, and `can_clear_prints?` — and remember the controller must enforce the
same rule, since hiding a button is not authorization.

For the logged-out public dashboard, use plain language and no internal jargon: no printer
IDs, no PrusaLink terminology, no audit timestamps.

## Component class reference

Defined in `refresh.scss` — use these rather than inventing new ones:

- `.h-page-title`, `.h-section-label` — typography
- `.text-11`, `.text-12`, `.text-13`, `.fw-medium` — type scale
- `.num` — tabular, right-aligned numerics
- `.status-dot` with `.status-success` / `.status-danger` / `.status-warning` / `.status-muted`
- `.filter-chip` with `.active`
- `.table-compact`
- `.job-timeline`, `.job-list-thumb`, `.job-list-thumbs-col` — job views
- `.dashboard-page`, `.dashboard-title`, `.dashboard-clock`, `.dashboard-printer-card`,
  `.dashboard-printer-name`, `.dashboard-job-filename`, `.dashboard-temps`,
  `.dashboard-image`, `.dashboard-image-placeholder`, `.dashboard-thumb`, `.dashboard-thumbs`,
  and the state modifiers `.dashboard-image-wrap--printing` / `--attention` / `--ready`

If a new pattern is genuinely needed, add it to `refresh.scss` — don't inline styles, and
don't reference classes that aren't in this list.

## Anti-patterns — never do these

- Multiple `btn-primary` buttons in one region.
- Saturated filled badges (`bg-success`, `bg-info`, …) for status — always `-subtle` variants.
- Numbered circles (1, 2, 3) on lists that aren't sequential steps.
- "Manage X" buttons inside a card titled "X".
- Full timestamps where relative dates would do.
- ALL CAPS for emphasis (use sentence case + `fw-medium`).
- Decorative emoji as primary icons — use Bootstrap Icons `bi-*`.
- Long explanatory paragraphs on index/landing pages.
- Hover effects with motion (scale transforms, glows). Subtle background changes only.
- Showing "0" or "None" / "Not provided" prominently. Mute zero states.
- Hardcoded hex colors that only read correctly in light or dark mode.

## Validation checklist

For any new page, verify:

- [ ] Color appears only where it encodes meaning.
- [ ] At most one `btn-primary`.
- [ ] Repeated values in columns are muted; outliers pop.
- [ ] Counts that need attention are surfaced inline.
- [ ] Body text 12-13px in tables; padding tight.
- [ ] Legible in both light and dark mode.
- [ ] Mobile collapses sensibly.
- [ ] Every tier-gated control is also enforced in the controller.
